{"name":"Double Infinity","hex":"#6f676b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"double","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made up of two matching or complementary elements.","Of twice the quantity."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Twice over; twofold; doubly.","Two together; two at a time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/double"},{"term":"infinity","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Endlessness, unlimitedness, absence of a beginning, end or limits to size.","A number that has an infinite numerical value that cannot be counted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infinity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Double Infinity","blocks":[{"text":"Double Infinity is the sixth studio album by the American indie rock band Big Thief, released on September 5, 2025, through 4AD. Produced and mixed by longtime collaborator Dom Monks, the album was recorded as a live band over the span of three weeks at the Power Station in New York City, with several session musicians contributing to the recording process."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8d/Big_Thief_-_Double_Infinity_%28cover_art%29.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double_Infinity"},{"title":"Infinity","blocks":[{"text":"Infinity is something which is boundless, limitless, or endless. It is denoted by ∞, called the infinity symbol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/SierpinskiTriangle.svg/330px-SierpinskiTriangle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infinity"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/N%C3%BAmeros_hiperreales.png/500px-N%C3%BAmeros_hiperreales.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/N%